WEBVTT

00:07.794 --> 00:10.127
together:
One, two, three, four.
一起：
一、二、三、四。

00:10.127 --> 00:11.894
I declare a thumb war!
我宣布拇指战争！

00:11.894 --> 00:14.627
[both straining]
[双方都紧张]

00:14.627 --> 00:16.661
[dramatic music]
[戏剧音乐]

00:16.661 --> 00:18.294
- Huh?
- Yah!
- 啊？
- 啊！

00:18.294 --> 00:20.894
[bell dinging]
[laughter]
[铃声]
[笑声]

00:20.894 --> 00:24.994
- Now that was
a great thumb war, mister.
- 现在那是
一场伟大的拇指战争，先生。

00:24.994 --> 00:28.061
- It was Patrick, but now
we will let peace prevail.
- 是帕特里克，但现在
我们将使和平占上风。

00:28.061 --> 00:29.194
Let us sign this treaty,
让我们签署这个条约，

00:29.194 --> 00:31.961
and our thumbs will live
in harmony.
我们的拇指会活下去
和谐地。

00:31.961 --> 00:33.727
[laughter]
[笑声]

00:33.727 --> 00:35.594
Great job, Patrick.
干得好，帕特里克。

00:35.594 --> 00:39.561
- Gee, thanks, SpongeBob.
That means a lot.
- 哎呀，谢谢，海绵宝宝。
这意味着很多。

00:39.561 --> 00:43.694
- Wow, giving someone
a thumbs-up feels great!
- 哇，给某人
竖起大拇指的感觉真好！

00:44.861 --> 00:47.361
- Boy, these Krabby Patties
are delicious.
- 男孩，这些蟹肉饼
很好吃。

00:47.361 --> 00:50.094
- I'll say.
They're absolutely stupendous.
- 我会说。
他们绝对是太棒了。

00:50.094 --> 00:54.561
- Well, you guys
are stupendous customers.
- 好吧，你们
都是很棒的客户。

00:54.561 --> 00:55.761
- [gasps]
- [喘气]

00:55.761 --> 00:57.927
That thumbs-up
really touched my heart.
那个竖起大拇指
真的触动了我的心。

00:57.927 --> 00:59.627
- Yeah, me too.
- 是的，我也是。

00:59.627 --> 01:02.594
It's like there's a thumbprint
of happiness on my aorta.
就像有指纹一样
我的主动脉上的幸福。

01:02.594 --> 01:04.827
[heart thumps]
[心跳]

01:04.827 --> 01:06.761
- [humming like a train]
- [像火车一样嗡嗡作响]

01:08.294 --> 01:09.461
Flipping.
翻转。

01:09.461 --> 01:11.827
- SpongeBob,
you shifty sea-slacker,
- 海绵宝宝，
你这个狡猾的懒鬼，

01:11.827 --> 01:14.727
have you counted the cups
like I told you to do?
你数过杯子了吗
就像我告诉你的那样？

01:14.727 --> 01:16.561
- I sure have, Mr. Krabs.
- 我当然有，蟹老板。

01:16.561 --> 01:17.827
Five.
五。

01:17.827 --> 01:19.627
But thanks for being
on top of the situation.
但谢谢你的存在
就目前情况而言。

01:19.627 --> 01:21.361
You're a fantastic boss.
你是一个很棒的老板。

01:21.361 --> 01:22.694
- Well, thank you.
- 嗯，谢谢。

01:22.694 --> 01:24.361
That's nice of you to say.
你说得真好。

01:24.361 --> 01:27.061
Now back to work!
现在回去工作吧！

01:27.061 --> 01:28.561
- Yes, sir!
- 是的，先生！

01:31.561 --> 01:33.061
- Oh, SpongeBob,
- 哦，海绵宝宝，

01:33.061 --> 01:36.327
do you have one of
your precious thumbs-up for me?
你有其中之一吗
你对我竖起大拇指吗？

01:36.327 --> 01:40.827
I would just love to get one.
[snickers]
我很想买一个。
[窃笑]

01:40.827 --> 01:44.961
- No, Squidward, I do not have
a thumbs-up for you.
- 不，章鱼哥，我没有
为你竖起大拇指。

01:46.561 --> 01:49.127
I've got two thumbs-up!
我竖起两个大拇指！

01:49.127 --> 01:52.394
- Oh.
That's...thank you.
- 哦。
那是……谢谢你。

01:52.394 --> 01:53.594
I think.
我认为。

01:53.594 --> 01:55.327
- [whistling]
- [吹口哨]

01:55.327 --> 01:56.661
Whoo!
呼！

01:58.794 --> 02:02.361
Hey, Sandy, I'm giving
your outfit two thumbs-up.
嘿，桑迪，我给
你的衣服竖起两个大拇指。

02:02.361 --> 02:04.027
- [giggles]
This old thing?
- [咯咯笑]
这老东西？

02:04.027 --> 02:05.861
It's just something I threw on.
这只是我扔在身上的东西。

02:05.861 --> 02:09.127
- Well, girl,
you really make it work.
- 好吧，女孩，
你真的让它发挥作用。

02:09.127 --> 02:11.561
- Okay.
- 好的。

02:11.561 --> 02:14.461
[laid-back music]
[悠闲的音乐]

02:14.461 --> 02:17.294
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

02:17.294 --> 02:19.994
- Excuse me, I'm trying
to find the Goo Lagoon
- 对不起，我正在努力
寻找古泻湖

02:19.994 --> 02:21.594
and I'm totally lost.
我完全迷路了。

02:21.594 --> 02:25.861
- Great job on not being afraid
to ask for directions.
- 做得很好，不害怕
询问方向。

02:25.861 --> 02:28.994
Hm...that way?
Okay.
嗯……这样？
好的。

02:30.594 --> 02:33.961
- You got the right stuff,
golden boys.
- 你得到了正确的东西，
金童。

02:33.961 --> 02:35.994
- SpongeBob, don't you think
that you may be using
- 海绵宝宝，你不觉得吗
您可能正在使用

02:35.994 --> 02:38.561
the thumbs-up
just a teensy bit too much?
竖起大拇指
只是有点太多了？

02:38.561 --> 02:40.194
- Are you kidding?
- 你在开玩笑吧？

02:40.194 --> 02:42.794
The thumbs-up is an iconic,
internationally-recognized sign
竖起大拇指是一种标志
国际公认的标志

02:42.794 --> 02:44.561
of positivity and affirmation.
的积极性和肯定性。

02:44.561 --> 02:46.127
Boop!
- Yeah, I know.
噗！
- 是的，我知道。

02:46.127 --> 02:49.327
But when you do it all the time,
the thumbs-up loses its meaning.
但当你一直这么做的时候
竖起大拇指就失去了意义。

02:49.327 --> 02:51.761
It becomes not special.
就变得不特别了。

02:51.761 --> 02:53.061
- Well, I happen to think
- 嗯，我碰巧想到

02:53.061 --> 02:56.361
you can never give
too many thumbs-up.
你永远无法给予
太多的竖起大拇指。

02:56.361 --> 02:57.861
- I don't know, SpongeBob.
- 我不知道，海绵宝宝。

02:57.861 --> 02:59.394
I think you should be careful.
我认为你应该小心。

02:59.394 --> 03:02.127
- Oh, Sandy, don't be
such a worry whale.
-哦，桑迪，别这样
真是一头忧心忡忡的鲸鱼。

03:02.127 --> 03:03.594
What could go wrong?
可能会出什么问题？

03:06.127 --> 03:08.194
[humming]
[嗡嗡声]

03:08.194 --> 03:09.427
Ah.
啊。

03:09.427 --> 03:12.994
Whoo, I'm giving away
thumbs-up today.
哇哦，我放弃了
今天竖起大拇指。

03:14.127 --> 03:17.394
Hey, guy.
Way to wait.
嘿，伙计。
等得好。

03:17.394 --> 03:18.894
- Who, me?
- 谁，我？

03:18.894 --> 03:21.027
[playful music]
[俏皮的音乐]

03:21.027 --> 03:24.561
Yeah...
[whistling]
是啊...
[吹口哨]

03:24.561 --> 03:29.994
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

03:29.994 --> 03:33.194
- Hey, guy.
Way to walk.
- 嘿，伙计。
走路的方式。

03:33.194 --> 03:34.327
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

03:34.327 --> 03:35.561
- [whimpers]
- [呜咽]

03:35.561 --> 03:36.661
[tires squealing]
[轮胎吱吱声]

03:36.661 --> 03:39.594
[thud]
- Oh, this feels great.
[砰]
- 哦，这感觉棒极了。

03:39.594 --> 03:44.894
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

03:44.894 --> 03:48.294
- Way to flick that eye booger--
- 甩掉那个眼屎的方法--

03:50.294 --> 03:51.694
[train whistles blowing]
[火车鸣笛]

03:51.694 --> 03:54.694
[dramatic music]
[戏剧音乐]

03:54.694 --> 03:56.027
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

03:56.027 --> 03:58.194
[cawing]
[啼叫]

03:58.194 --> 04:00.194
[baby crying]
[婴儿哭声]

04:00.194 --> 04:01.761
- Thumbhawk one.
Thumbhawk one.
- 拇指鹰一号。
拇指鹰一。

04:01.761 --> 04:03.061
This is Thumbhawk two.
We got two thumbs down.
这是拇指鹰二号。
我们有两个大拇指朝下。

04:03.061 --> 04:04.661
Repeat.
Two thumbs down!
重复。
两个大拇指朝下！

04:04.661 --> 04:06.561
- Thumbhawk one here, copy that.
- 这里有拇指鹰，复制它。

04:06.561 --> 04:08.061
Initiate emergency procedures.
启动紧急程序。

04:08.061 --> 04:09.794
- Initiating on my count.
- 从我的计数开始。

04:09.794 --> 04:11.561
Three, two, one.
三、二、一。

04:11.561 --> 04:13.861
[screaming]
[尖叫]

04:13.861 --> 04:16.994
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

04:16.994 --> 04:19.561
- Oh, my thumbs.
My thumbs!
- 哦，我的拇指。
我的大拇指！

04:19.561 --> 04:23.694
My thumbs!
我的大拇指！

04:27.927 --> 04:29.727
How's it looking, Dr. Manfish?
曼菲什博士，看起来怎么样？

04:29.727 --> 04:32.727
- Well, I'm afraid it
doesn't look good, SpongeBob.
- 好吧，我担心
看起来不太好，海绵宝宝。

04:32.727 --> 04:36.227
It seems you've severely damaged
your ulnar collateral ligament,
看来你已经严重受损了
你的尺侧副韧带，

04:36.227 --> 04:39.461
possible from
some kind of repeated action.
可能来自
某种重复的动作。

04:39.461 --> 04:41.827
- An action like a thumbs-up?
- 像竖起大拇指这样的动作？

04:41.827 --> 04:43.561
- Certainly
that is one possibility.
- 当然
这是一种可能性。

04:43.561 --> 04:45.161
Hitchhiking could be another.
搭便车可能是另一种情况。

04:45.161 --> 04:47.727
- But doctor, I will be able
to use my thumbs again, right?
- 但是医生，我会的
再次使用我的拇指，对吗？

04:49.461 --> 04:52.294
- SpongeBob,
I can't say that for certain.
- 海绵宝宝，
我不能肯定地说。

04:52.294 --> 04:54.694
I'm only a board certified
thumbologist.
我只是获得董事会认证的人
拇指学家。

04:54.694 --> 04:56.227
I don't know everything.
我不知道一切。

04:56.227 --> 04:59.427
I can only say that we must
give it time and see.
我只能说我们必须
给它时间看看。

04:59.427 --> 05:01.061
There are limits to science.
科学是有局限性的。

05:01.061 --> 05:03.327
But you should prepare yourself
for the possibility
但你应该做好准备
为了可能性

05:03.327 --> 05:07.294
that you may never regain
the use of your thumbs again.
你可能永远无法恢复
再次使用拇指。

05:10.261 --> 05:11.561
- [coughing]
- [咳嗽]

05:13.127 --> 05:16.661
- All right, you boneless
invertebrate lazy bones...
- 好吧，你这个没骨头的人
无脊椎动物的懒骨头...

05:16.661 --> 05:18.161
[chuckles]
Come on.
[笑声]
来吧。

05:18.161 --> 05:21.427
Flip them patties, boy-o,
just like the old days.
翻转他们的肉饼，男孩，哦，
就像过去一样。

05:21.427 --> 05:23.894
- Aye aye, Mr. Krabs.
- 是啊是啊，蟹老板。

05:26.761 --> 05:28.561
[straining]
[紧张]

05:30.227 --> 05:32.427
- Uh, let me give you a hand.
My thumbs work.
- 呃，让我帮你一把。
我的拇指可以工作。

05:32.427 --> 05:34.394
- No!
I can do it.
- 不！
我能做到。

05:35.627 --> 05:38.427
[groans]
[呻吟]

05:41.794 --> 05:44.161
[straining]
[紧张]

05:44.161 --> 05:45.561
[slap]
[拍击]

05:48.161 --> 05:51.827
- I'm sorry, son, but I have
a business to run.
- 对不起，儿子，但我已经
经营一家企业。

05:51.827 --> 05:53.227
I'm gonna have to let you go.
我得让你走。

05:53.227 --> 05:56.194
- That's okay, Mr. Krabs.
I understand.
- 没关系，蟹老板。
我明白。

05:56.194 --> 05:59.127
- Now where's me
new fry cook?
- 现在我在哪里
新炒菜厨师？

05:59.127 --> 06:01.327
There he is!
Come on in here.
他在那儿！
进来吧。

06:01.327 --> 06:02.861
- [straining]
- [紧张]

06:02.861 --> 06:05.127
[grill sizzling]
[烧烤滋滋作响]

06:05.127 --> 06:07.861
Uh, sorry, SpongeBob.
呃，对不起，海绵宝宝。

06:10.327 --> 06:12.094
- Patrick, I'm glad it's you.
- 帕特里克，我很高兴是你。

06:12.094 --> 06:14.427
Better than some
weird stranger, right?
比一些好
奇怪的陌生人，对吧？

06:14.427 --> 06:17.261
- Uh, yeah, I guess.
- 呃，是的，我想。

06:17.261 --> 06:22.061
I probably won't even be able
to do good flipping.
我可能甚至无法
做好翻转。

06:22.061 --> 06:25.094
- With a little practice,
you could do anything.
- 经过一点练习，
你可以做任何事。

06:25.094 --> 06:28.294
[groans]
Oh...
[呻吟]
哦...

06:28.294 --> 06:29.994
[all gasp]
[全都喘气]

06:29.994 --> 06:32.161
- Ol' Patty flippin' patties.
- 老帕蒂翻转肉饼。

06:32.161 --> 06:33.627
Who'd a' thunk it, huh?
谁会想到它，嗯？

06:33.627 --> 06:35.294
[all laugh sadly]
[大家悲伤地笑]

06:35.294 --> 06:36.427
- Poor kid.
- 可怜的孩子。

06:37.727 --> 06:39.394
[somber music]
[忧郁的音乐]

06:39.394 --> 06:42.127
- * Thumbs are opposable,
thumbs are great *
- * 拇指是相对的，
拇指很棒*

06:42.127 --> 06:45.194
* We share them with
the monkeys and with the apes *
* 我们与以下人士分享
猴子和猿 *

06:45.194 --> 06:48.227
* You can grab, you can tie,
you can pinch a cheek *
* 你可以抓，你可以系，
你可以捏一下脸颊*

06:48.227 --> 06:51.561
all: * But without your thumbs,
you're all thumbs *
所有人：*但是没有你的拇指，
你们都竖起大拇指*

06:51.561 --> 06:53.294
* All thumbs,
no thumbs *
*所有的拇指，
没有大拇指 *

06:53.294 --> 06:55.127
* Busted up your thumbs
*竖起大拇指

06:55.127 --> 06:57.661
* Sucking on your pinkie
would sure look dumb *
*吮吸你的小指
肯定看起来很蠢*

06:57.661 --> 07:00.961
- * You'll never hitch a ride
or pull out a plum *
- * 你永远不会搭便车
或者拔出一个李子*

07:00.961 --> 07:04.161
all: * Without your thumbs,
you're all thumbs *
全部：*没有你的拇指，
你们都竖起大拇指*

07:04.161 --> 07:05.627
- * Thumbs, thumbs
- * 拇指，拇指

07:05.627 --> 07:07.727
all: * All thumbs,
no thumbs *
全部：* 全部竖起大拇指，
没有大拇指 *

07:07.727 --> 07:09.394
* Feels like a crime
* 感觉像是犯罪

07:09.394 --> 07:11.994
* Can't pull on a zipper
or flip a dime *
* 拉链拉不上
或翻转一毛钱 *

07:11.994 --> 07:13.561
* And forget about chopsticks
*忘记筷子

07:13.561 --> 07:15.427
* You'll starve every time *
*每次你都会挨饿*

07:15.427 --> 07:17.894
* Without your thumbs,
you're all thumbs *
*没有你的拇指，
你们都竖起大拇指*

07:17.894 --> 07:20.127
- * Thumbs, thumbs, thumbs
- * 拇指，拇指，拇指

07:20.127 --> 07:23.127
all: * Thumbs, thumbs, thumbs
全部： * 大拇指，大拇指，大拇指

07:23.127 --> 07:27.027
- * Without your thumbs
- * 没有你的拇指

07:27.027 --> 07:31.294
* You're all thumbs *
*你们都是大拇指*

07:31.294 --> 07:32.594
- [whispering]
Thumbs, thumbs, thumbs.
- [低语]
大拇指，大拇指，大拇指。

07:32.594 --> 07:35.327
- [knocking]
SpongeBob, it's me, Sandy!
- [敲门声]
海绵宝宝，是我，桑迪！

07:35.327 --> 07:38.094
Hey, SpongeBob!
I haven't seen you in days.
嘿，海绵宝宝！
我已经好几天没见到你了。

07:38.094 --> 07:41.027
What'cha doin'?
- Waiting for autumn.
你在做什么？
- 等待秋天。

07:41.027 --> 07:43.361
- Come now,
it can't be that bad.
- 来吧，
事情不可能那么糟糕。

07:43.361 --> 07:45.827
- Leave me, Sandra.
Forget you ever knew me.
- 离开我，桑德拉。
忘记你曾经认识我。

07:45.827 --> 07:49.661
Erase from your memory the face
of this useless sponge
从你的记忆中抹去这张脸
这个无用的海绵

07:49.661 --> 07:52.694
with these mutilated thumbs!
用这些残缺的拇指！

07:52.694 --> 07:55.261
- [gasps]
Don't give up, SpongeBob!
- [喘气]
不要放弃，海绵宝宝！

07:55.261 --> 07:57.794
You have to find
something you love.
你必须找到
你喜欢的东西。

07:57.794 --> 07:59.427
Something to live for.
为之而活的东西。

07:59.427 --> 08:01.861
- Ha.
And what might that be?
- 哈。
那可能是什么？

08:01.861 --> 08:03.361
- I don't know, SpongeBob.
- 我不知道，海绵宝宝。

08:03.361 --> 08:07.461
That's a question
you have to answer for yourself.
这是一个问题
你必须自己回答。

08:07.461 --> 08:10.461
[somber music]
[忧郁的音乐]

08:10.461 --> 08:11.494
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

08:11.494 --> 08:13.661
- Sandy?
Sandy.
- 桑迪？
沙。

08:13.661 --> 08:15.794
Sandy, come back!
桑迪，回来吧！

08:15.794 --> 08:19.694
I need you to help me open
this jar of peanut butter!
我需要你帮我打开
这罐花生酱！

08:19.694 --> 08:22.361
[straining]
[紧张]

08:22.361 --> 08:25.494
[glass shattering]
[sobbing]
[玻璃破碎]
[抽泣]

08:27.094 --> 08:30.061
Enough sitting around
feeling sorry for myself.
坐够了
为自己感到难过。

08:30.061 --> 08:33.061
[inspirational music]
【励志音乐】

08:33.061 --> 08:41.061
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

08:41.061 --> 08:42.927
[straining]
[紧张]

08:42.927 --> 08:47.727
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

08:47.727 --> 08:50.727
- [shouting]
- [喊叫]

08:50.727 --> 08:53.661
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

08:54.894 --> 08:56.827
- Um...
- 嗯...

08:56.827 --> 08:59.427
Oof.
Turn over.
钱币。
翻。

08:59.427 --> 09:00.961
[meat sizzling]
[肉滋滋作响]

09:00.961 --> 09:03.861
- My thumbs are better,
and I am ready to work.
- 我的拇指好多了
我已经准备好工作了。

09:03.861 --> 09:05.461
- The job's taken.
- 工作被抢走了。

09:05.461 --> 09:07.461
- Well, I'm taking it back.
- 好吧，我收回它。

09:07.461 --> 09:10.061
- Just how you gonna do that?
- 你要怎么做？

09:10.061 --> 09:12.094
[dramatic music]
[戏剧音乐]

09:12.094 --> 09:13.727
- Thumb war.
- 拇指战争。

09:13.727 --> 09:15.094
- En garde.
- 前卫。

09:15.094 --> 09:17.194
together:
One, two, three, four.
一起：
一、二、三、四。

09:17.194 --> 09:19.561
I declare a thumb war!
我宣布拇指战争！

09:19.561 --> 09:21.227
[swords clanking]
[刀剑叮当作响]

09:21.227 --> 09:24.927
[both grunting and straining]
[咕噜声和紧张]

09:24.927 --> 09:33.061
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

09:35.027 --> 09:36.561
- Whoa!
- 哇！

09:36.561 --> 09:38.561
[all gasp]
[全都喘气]

09:38.561 --> 09:39.761
[swords clanking]
[刀剑叮当作响]

09:39.761 --> 09:42.361
- Ooh.
[shouts]
- 哦。
[喊叫]

09:42.361 --> 09:45.361
Admit it.
You have been bested.
承认吧。
你已经被打败了。

09:45.361 --> 09:46.761
- Never.
- 绝不。

09:46.761 --> 09:50.061
*
*
*
*
*
*
*
*

09:50.061 --> 09:52.461
- Then prepare to be pinned.
- 然后准备被钉住。

09:52.461 --> 09:54.094
- [groaning]
- Don't give up.
- [呻吟]
- 不要放弃。

09:54.094 --> 09:55.794
Something to live for.
为之而活的东西。

09:55.794 --> 09:58.694
all: Something to live for!
所有人：活着的目的！

09:58.694 --> 10:00.727
- [sucking]
- [吸吮]

10:03.594 --> 10:05.027
[swords clanking]
[刀剑叮当作响]

10:05.027 --> 10:07.027
all: Whoa!
全体：哇！

10:07.027 --> 10:08.894
[both straining]
[双方都紧张]

10:08.894 --> 10:10.127
[swords clash]
- Yeah!
[刀剑交锋]
- 是啊！

10:10.127 --> 10:12.894
- SpongeBob wins!
- 海绵宝宝赢了！

10:12.894 --> 10:14.294
[all cheering]
[大家欢呼]

10:14.294 --> 10:17.627
- SpongeBob,
you old patty jockey.
- 海绵宝宝，
你这个老帕蒂骑师。

10:17.627 --> 10:20.194
Welcome home, son.
欢迎回家，儿子。

10:20.194 --> 10:23.561
- Uh, it's okay.
I hate work anyway.
- 呃，没关系。
反正我讨厌工作。

10:23.561 --> 10:25.161
[laughter]
[笑声]

10:25.161 --> 10:26.327
- Oh, Patrick.
- 哦，帕特里克。

10:26.327 --> 10:28.827
- No, but really,
I do hate work.
- 不，但实际上，
我确实讨厌工作。

10:28.827 --> 10:31.761
[laughter]
[笑声]

10:32.827 --> 10:35.227
- [laughing]
- [笑]

10:35.227 --> 10:37.827
Everybody's laughing!
大家都在笑！

10:37.827 --> 10:39.261
Oh, hey, SpongeBob.
哦，嘿，海绵宝宝。

10:39.261 --> 10:40.961
I got something for you.
我有东西给你。

10:40.961 --> 10:42.094
- Yes, Patrick?
- 是的，帕特里克？

10:42.094 --> 10:44.861
[mellow music]
[柔和的音乐]

10:44.861 --> 10:46.894
all: Ooh.
全体：噢。

10:46.894 --> 10:49.227
[all cheering]
[大家欢呼]

10:49.227 --> 10:51.794
[fireworks exploding]
[烟花爆炸]

[烟花爆炸]